      "summary": "The investigator’s pre-call token guard can undercount tool results and send a request above the required input-token limit. The remaining stated limit and trace behaviors have corresponding coverage in the changed test file.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "backend/AirlineDemo.Api/Investigation/BoundedInvestigator.cs",
          "line": 325,
          "message": "The pre-call input limit estimate omits function-result content, so an over-limit request can reach the model before the actual usage check detects the breach.",
          "confidence": 0.94,
          "category": "logic-error",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "GatedModelClient.EstimateInputBytes counts ChatMessage.Text and tool schemas. Tool results are carried in FunctionResultContent, which is not included in the text estimate; actual input usage is checked only after the model responds.",
            "failureScenario": "A read tool returns a large source page as a function result. The next model request's estimate omits that result, so it can exceed the 16,000-token limit and still be sent; the breach is detected only after the model processes it."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
