      "summary": "The tests cover the listed limit breaches and both trace outcomes. The input-token estimate still misses function-call content in model history, leaving a reachable path that sends an over-limit request.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "backend/AirlineDemo.Api/Investigation/BoundedInvestigator.cs",
          "line": 323,
          "message": "The input-token guard omits non-text message content, including function-call arguments, so a later tool-loop request can exceed the per-call limit before the breach is detected.",
          "confidence": 0.85,
          "category": "logic-error",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "GatedModelClient.EstimateInputBytes counts only ChatMessage.Text and declared tool schemas. After a tool call, the next model request can include FunctionCallContent arguments in the message history, which this estimate omits; actual usage is checked only after the model responds.",
            "failureScenario": "A model returns a large function-call payload, and the following request includes that payload alongside text near the 16,000-token limit. The estimate can remain under the cap while the actual request exceeds it, so the over-limit request reaches the model."
          }
        }
      ]
